KG42.register("source_edge_archive-9138b57623f97d819d369704",{"id":"16-cooperative_microgrid_incentives::v141-c-R002::E::v141-c-R002-E001","paper":"16-cooperative_microgrid_incentives","rule_id":"v141-c-R002","rule_ref":"16-cooperative_microgrid_incentives::v141-c-R002","record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R002-E001","source":"coordination.price_signal","target":"clearing.social_welfare","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R002-C001","v141-c-R002-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e027","v141-b-g02-e028","v141-b-g04-E24","v141-b-g04-E25"]},"evidence_class":"S","provenance_gate":"direct_C_edge_with_constraint_and_source_excerpt","scientific_acceptance":false,"accepted_constraint_ids":["v141-c-R002-C001","v141-c-R002-C002"],"held_constraint_ids":[],"semantic_review_status":"supported","source":"COMP-259000fdd3b58453","target":"COMP-13ec024ac7c1d3de","source_occurrence_id":"16-cooperative_microgrid_incentives::v141-c-R002::V::coordination.price_signal","target_occurrence_id":"16-cooperative_microgrid_incentives::v141-c-R002::V::clearing.social_welfare","source_unit_id":"16-cooperative_microgrid_incentives::v141-a-M01::coordination.price_signal","target_unit_id":"16-cooperative_microgrid_incentives::v141-a-M01::clearing.social_welfare","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"clearing","context_text":"Coalition {Private investor, D}: iterative solution of the microgrid's surplus-maximizing allocation problem alongside the utility's separate optimization. | Coalition {Private investor, D}: joint optimization for the private investor and customers at node D. | Coalition {VIU, Private investor, D}: joint optimization of the utility, private investor and customers at node D. | Coalition {VIU, Private investor, D}: regulated-price iteration for the grand-coalition dispatch model.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e027","v141-b-g02-e028","v141-b-g04-E16","v141-b-g04-E24","v141-b-g04-E25"]},"active":true,"source_signature":"756f074de09c1b79daae95cf97e317f708955c410a6afdadc2809dd8a9745333","relation_scope":"original_occurrence_pair_only","internal_to_parent":false,"source_science":{"mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","source_definition":"Repeat regulated-price updates and consumers’ responses, with the models solved again for power dispatch, until convergence is achieved. Scope: Numerical equilibrium solution for Coalitions {VIU}, {D}, {VIU, D}, {VIU, Private investor} and {VIU, Private investor, D}. Repeat the separate utility–microgrid decision iteration, in which the microgrid updates its decisions in response to the resulting regulated utility price, until convergence is achieved. Scope: Numerical equilibrium solution for Coalition {Private investor, D}, with separate utility and microgrid optimization models. Regulators may introduce feed-in premiums on top of market prices to promote microgrid development and efficient operation, including higher production at peak hours. Scope: Proposed regulatory incentives for microgrid development and efficient operation.","target_definition":"The regulated-price signal feeds the microgrid's optimization of generation, imports and reactive power under the coalition's benefit-minus-cost objective; the microgrid updates its decisions using the resulting utility price. Scope: Coalition {Private investor, D}: iterative solution of the microgrid's surplus-maximizing allocation problem alongside the utility's separate optimization. Condition: The utility's regulated price is treated as fixed during each microgrid optimization and updated between iterations. Regulated-price coordination feeds successive solutions of the grand-coalition surplus-maximizing dispatch model: consumers revise their decisions given the price and the model is solved again for optimal power dispatch. Scope: Coalition {VIU, Private investor, D}: regulated-price iteration for the grand-coalition dispatch model. Condition: During successive regulated-price and dispatch iterations. The allocation objective maximizes gross electricity-consumption benefit at the distribution nodes minus generation, power-import, new-capacity and grid-connection costs, subject to distribution-node Kirchhoff's Current Law and microgrid generator and load constraints. Generation costs include consumer expenditures for heat not supplied by microgrid generators. Scope: Coalition {Private investor, D}: joint optimization for the private investor and customers at node D. Condition: Applicable to this coalition's optimization; the utility optimizes separately. The allocation objective maximizes the three players' total surplus subject to network and generator constraints. It includes gross electricity-consumption benefit at distribution nodes and power-sales revenues at all nodes, less generation, reserve, new-capacity, microgrid-connection and depreciation costs and the allowed return on investment. Scope: Coalition {VIU, Private investor, D}: joint optimization of the utility, private investor and customers at node D. Condition: Applicable to the grand-coalition optimization.","constraints":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R002-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The regulated-price signal feeds the microgrid's optimization of generation, imports and reactive power under the coalition's benefit-minus-cost objective; the microgrid updates its decisions using the resulting utility price. Scope: Coalition {Private investor, D}: iterative solution of the microgrid's surplus-maximizing allocation problem alongside the utility's separate optimization. Condition: The utility's regulated price is treated as fixed during each microgrid optimization and updated between iterations.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.price_signal","clearing.social_welfare"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e027","v141-b-g04-E25"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R002-C002","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Regulated-price coordination feeds successive solutions of the grand-coalition surplus-maximizing dispatch model: consumers revise their decisions given the price and the model is solved again for optimal power dispatch. Scope: Coalition {VIU, Private investor, D}: regulated-price iteration for the grand-coalition dispatch model. Condition: During successive regulated-price and dispatch iterations.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.price_signal","clearing.social_welfare"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e028","v141-b-g04-E24"]}],"evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e027","location":{"location_id":"src-43db3c92a3-p08-c1r2__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":8,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"for its sales to local customers. Given the regulated price, the pri- vate investor can earn a proﬁt","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-08.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"For Coalition {Private investor, D}, we present the joint model of the private investor and the consumers at distribution nodes, as well as the model for the utility. The reason for presenting a model for a non-member of the coalition is that, unlike most cooperative game analyses, the value of Coalition {Private investor, D} depends on the utility’s actions. The utility and the microgrid take decisions separately, but each decision influences what the other party does in reaction and affects each other’s surplus; as a result, it is necessary to consider the utility’s problem as well. The goal of the private investor and customers at node D is to maximize the gross benefit of electricity consumption at the distribution nodes, minus costs for generation, power imports, new installed capacity and connection to the grid. The objective function is subject to Kirchhoff’s Current Law at the distribution nodes, plus generator and load constraints in the MG. On the other hand, the utility’s goal is to maximize profits, subject to network and central generation capacity constraints. No power is exported from the MG to the main grid, while distribution expansion represents only a parameter for the MG, as it is determined in the VIU’s problem. Finally, the MG treats the regulated electricity price as fixed, while electricity exports and MG generation are given in the VIU’s problem."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e028","location":{"location_id":"src-43db3c92a3-p08-c1r3__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":8,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"hoff’s Current Law at the distribution nodes, plus generator and load constraints in the MG. On the ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-08.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The objective of Coalition {VIU, Private investor, D} is to maximize the total surplus of the three players, subject to network and generator constraints. The objective function includes the gross benefit of electricity consumption at the distribution nodes and revenues from power sales at all nodes, minus costs for generation, reserves, new installed capacity and MG connection to the grid, depreciation expenses and allowed return on investment."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g04-E24","location":{"location_id":"src-43db3c92a3-p17-c1r2__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":17,"printed_page":"540","section":"Appendix C. Solution approach","anchor_text":"y g y q y sales (Eq. (3)). Thus, ﬁnding the equilibrium price and quantities is a ﬁxed point problem","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-17.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"In Coalitions {VIU}, {D}, {VIU, D}, {VIU, Private investor} and {VIU, Private investor, D}, given an initial value for P, customers determine their consumption (equal to the utility’s sales), Q(P), and the model is solved to obtain the optimal power dispatch in the network. Then, a new regulated electricity price, P(Q), is obtained, based on the new level of sales and costs. Given the price, consumers modify their decisions and the models are solved again to find the optimal power dispatch. The last two steps are repeated until convergence is achieved. Note that in Coalitions {VIU, Private investor} and {VIU, Private investor, D} the regulated price is set to recover the utility’s costs only, since the private investor is not subject to cost-of-service regulation."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g04-E25","location":{"location_id":"src-43db3c92a3-p17-c1r3__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":17,"printed_page":"540","section":"Appendix C. Solution approach","anchor_text":"} { , , } g p [17 recover the utility’s costs only, since the private investor is not sub- ject to c","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-17.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Solving Coalition {Private investor, D} introduces an additional complexity: the utility and the microgrid take decisions separately, but these decisions influence each other. Their optimization models are solved iteratively. In the first step, given an initial value for the utility’s regulated price, the microgrid optimizes electricity generation, imports from the main grid and reactive power production; the MG treats the utility’s regulated price as fixed. In the second step, the utility optimizes power dispatch in the network, given the microgrid’s quantity decisions; the VIU treats MG exports and generation as fixed. The microgrid successively updates its decisions based on the resulting regulated price for the utility. These steps are repeated until convergence is achieved. Searching for the equilibrium can still be thought of as solving a fixed point problem, where Q^{-1}(P) are the MG’s power imports from the microgrid’s problem. The regulated electricity price depends on Q, the total utility’s sales, that include the microgrid’s imports decisions (Q^{-1}(P)), as well as sales at the other nodes of the network."}],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"clearing","context_text":"Coalition {Private investor, D}: iterative solution of the microgrid's surplus-maximizing allocation problem alongside the utility's separate optimization. | Coalition {Private investor, D}: joint optimization for the private investor and customers at node D. | Coalition {VIU, Private investor, D}: joint optimization of the utility, private investor and customers at node D. | Coalition {VIU, Private investor, D}: regulated-price iteration for the grand-coalition dispatch model.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e027","v141-b-g02-e028","v141-b-g04-E16","v141-b-g04-E24","v141-b-g04-E25"]},"source_record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R002-E001","source":"coordination.price_signal","target":"clearing.social_welfare","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R002-C001","v141-c-R002-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e027","v141-b-g02-e028","v141-b-g04-E24","v141-b-g04-E25"]},"paper_scope_note":"Different alliances and fixed-point steps are retained separately; the original text explicitly states that convergence is not guaranteed, and price feedback cannot be described as having guaranteed equilibrium."}});
